    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273-a5">

                <pb facs="0505" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 5 in No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Lord Lyons to Major General Doyle.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit to your
                    excellency copies of four despatches which I have addressed to Earl Russell,
                    with regard to the affair of the Chesapeake.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d273-f1"/></p>
                <p>These papers will make your excellency fully acquainted with the communications
                    which I have had on the subject with the United States government since I had
                    the honor to write to your excellency on the 21st ultimo.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
